From cf543a820456cf3642d04b7c49017d473b53ea17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 12:33:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: the Failover tab - the resolver health check and the
 dnsmasq switches leave the System page

Owner request 2026-09-07: everything the v3.1.1 rung added to Administration >
System (the Reaper resolver health check with its eight fields, and the three
dnsmasq switches: strict upstream order, EDNS Client Subnet, no router cache)
moves to its own tab, Failover, between System and Firmware Upgrade, designed
as a lightweight Reaper-native page in the router's theme.

- www/Reaper_Failover.asp (new, native, self-themed like Reaper_Backup): the
  sigil header with two live chips (state with a pulsing dot - jade answering,
  crimson not answering, steel off - and the watched server), a three-step
  Watch / Fail over / Restore strip whose middle step ARMS while the server is
  down, the health check in a hero card with a neutral-grey enable switch and
  its fields (the card dims while off), one card per dnsmasq switch, one Apply.
  The state is polled every 5 s through the stock appGet nvram hook; settings
  go through the stock apply flow (start_apply.htm in a hidden frame) with
  restart_rdnshc and/or restart_dnsmasq as action_script, then the page
  reloads. Validation as before: IPv4 always, IPv6 only while ipv6_service is
  on, name charset, the four ranges. ASCII-only, tokens in backtick JS only.
- Advanced_System_Content.asp: the block, its JS, the apply hook, the validate
  hook and the five hidden inputs are gone; the page no longer mentions the
  keys at all.
- require/menuTrees/menuTree.js (rule 20 file): the tab after System.
- httpd/reaper_inject.c: the page in reaper_native[] (bounce only).
- Tokens RDHC_28..39 (tab name, subtitle, the three step names and captions,
  the applying line, Off / Answering / Not answering) translated in all 25
  packs, lockstep 6907. reaper_langcheck.py page list gains the page (engine +
  lean copy).

Gates: reaper_static_checks 11/11; the page script resolved through every
pack passes node --check (25/25); mk-httpd clean; verify markers added
(page literals present, System page literals ABSENT, httpd + installed menu).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
